<p>Hey, we are ConOps, a team of 4 Directors and currently over 45 members, and you could be one of them!</p>
<p>Ever wondered what it's like to work at a convention? Or do you want to volunteer at Eurofurence but have no idea which department is right for you? ConOps is your way to go! We offer many different tasks, cooperation with other departments, and a big look behind the scenes. If something needs doing and nobody else is doing it, that's probably us.</p>

<h3>What do we do?</h3>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Info Desk:</strong> We organize and coordinate the Eurofurence Info Desk. Together with other departments like Critter Operations and Awareness & Inclusion, we staff the Info Desk, the single front desk for all non-medical and non-security related questions about the services and rooms of Eurofurence.</li>
    <li><strong>Locker Service:</strong> We help our attendees by taking care of their belongings, so they can roam around the convention freely, whether they need to store bags before entering the Dealers' Den, the Art Show, or just want to walk around without carrying everything.</li>
    <li><strong>Room Management:</strong> Ever wondered who makes the magic behind smoothly running panels? Changing room layouts, installing tech equipment like PA systems or projectors? That's us! Together with Stage Tech and Programming, we make all the panels happen.</li>
    <li><strong>Internal Services:</strong> The glue that holds everything together behind the scenes, and sometimes in front of them. From distributing seat reservations for staff so they can head straight from their shift to a show, to our On Duty Team: a special task group that's always ready to jump in and help wherever an extra pair of hands is needed. No two days are the same!</li>
</ul>

<h3>Joining ConOps</h3>

<p>When you join ConOps, you don't just join one team, you become part of the whole department. We encourage everyone to try different roles. Using our self-scheduling tool, you pick the shifts that work for you across all our services. We only step in if shifts still need filling. We expect around 4-5 hours per day you're at the convention, typically adding up to about 15-20 hours across the convention days (Wednesday to Saturday).</p>
<p>We ask our team members to arrive by Tuesday morning to help with setup and to be available on Sunday for teardown. Setup and teardown are an all-hands effort: regardless of your usual role, everyone pitches in to get the convention up and running (and packed away again). How much you contribute on those days is up to you, every pair of hands helps!</p>
<p>You must be a registered attendee of Eurofurence and meet the convention's minimum age requirement. No prior convention or staffing experience is needed. We provide manuals and process documentation, and our experienced team members ("Council") and a Director on Duty are always available to help.</p>
<p>Being fluent in English is required for most of our positions.</p>
<p>There is no application deadline, you can reach out to us at any time. We'll have a short, informal chat to get to know each other, learn about your interests and skills, and figure out where you'd fit best.</p>

<h3>Why join ConOps?</h3>

<ul>
    <li>Help make this convention happen. Eurofurence is entirely volunteer-run!</li>
    <li>Look behind the scenes and have the opportunity to influence how things are done</li>
    <li>Access to the staff lounge (with slushies, soft ice, cup noodles, real food, and more)</li>
    <li>Our own ConOps back office with drinks, exclusive to the team</li>
    <li>A small token of appreciation for every team member each year</li>
    <li>A great team with great team spirit</li>
</ul>

<h3>Interested?</h3>

<p>A simple “Hi, I’m interested!” is enough to get started, a short introduction about yourself is also welcome. Please send us an email to <a href="mailto:ConOps@Eurofurence.org" target="_blank">ConOps@Eurofurence.org</a> or contact <a href="https://t.me/FurryTeddyBear" target="_blank">@FurryTeddyBear on Telegram</a>. Email is slightly preferred for initial contact; we usually continue the conversation on Telegram. While we strongly prefer applications before the convention, feel free to reach out to us if you’re interested, even on short notice.</p>